<title>UK: Deutsche unit sets 400 mln Dkr step-up bond.</title>
<headline>Deutsche unit sets 400 mln Dkr step-up bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Deutsche Morgan Grenfell and Kredietbank.</p>
<p> BORROWER   DEUTSCHE BANK FINANCE</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  DEUTSCHE BANK AG (AAA/AA1)</p>
<p> AMT    400 MLN DKR   COUPON     *5.0	MATURITY    27.MAY.05</p>
<p> TYPE   STEP-UP	 ISS PRICE  101.68    PAY DATE    27.MAY.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.00	REOFFER    =	   SPREAD	+5 BP</p>
<p> LISTING    GERMAN    DENOMS (K) 10-50     SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    GERMAN    HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.625     SELL CONC  1.375     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 15 PCT 2004 DANISH GOVERNMENT BOND</p>
<p> NOTES	*FOR FIRST FOUR YEARS THEN STEPS-UP TO 8.0 PCT</p>
<p> THEREAFTER</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
